# Shared Circuit Understanding Document (SCUD): power-circuit

## 1. Circuit Overview & System Context
The `power-circuit` is the primary high-voltage and isolation interface of the `stackable-bms` system. It integrates five specialized modules to provide battery monitoring, current sensing, low-side power switching, isolated communication, and internal power distribution.

**Integration Strategy:**
- **Sensing:** The `BMM` handles cell-level voltage and temperature, while the `CS` module monitors total pack current via a shunt integrated into the `SWC`.
- **Power Control:** The `SWC` performs low-side power switching for charge and discharge paths and provides the Kelvin sense taps for current measurement.
- **Communication:** The `CB` serves as the gateway between the low-voltage control domain and the high-voltage daisy chain.
- **Power:** The `HVPS` converts traction bus voltage into regulated logic power for the isolated sensing front-end and the gate drivers of the switching circuit.

## 2. Architectural Deviations & Integration Logic
- **Isolated Power Domain (VDD1_ISO):** To ensure reliable current sensing even when the main BMS monitor might be in a low-power state or fault, the `HVPS` is designated as the primary provider for the `CS` module's hot-side power (`VDD1`).
    - *Logic:* `HVPS.VDD1` (5.0V) is connected to `CS.VDD1`.
- **Gate Drive Power (VDD_12V_ISO):** The `HVPS` provides an isolated 12V rail specifically for the gate drivers in the `SWC`.
    - *Logic:* `HVPS.VDD12V` is connected to `SWC.VDD_12V`.
- **Integrated Current Sensing:** Current sensing is performed via a 1.0mΩ shunt resistor located within the `SWC`. The Kelvin sense taps (`SRP/SRN`) are routed directly to the `CS` module.
    - *Logic:* `SWC.SRP/SRN` <-> `CS.INP/INN`.
- **Daisy Chain Topology:** The `CB` is configured as the daisy chain master. Its High-side communication port (`COMH`) is connected to the Low-side port (`COM_L`) of the first `BMM` in the stack.
    - *Logic:* `CB.COMH_P/N` <-> `BMM.COM_LP/N`.
- **Ground Referencing:** The High-Voltage Negative (HV-) traction bus serves as the common reference (`GND_HV`) for the `HVPS`, the `CS` hot-side, the `SWC` hot-side, and the negative terminal of the 16-cell battery stack.

## 3. Comprehensive Components Inventory
The `power-circuit` consists of five integrated specialized modules and their supporting interconnects:
- **Module 1:** `bms-monitor-module` (BMM) - Stackable 16-cell monitoring and balancing.
- **Module 2:** `communication-bridge` (CB) - Isolated SPI/UART to daisy-chain gateway.
- **Module 3:** `current-sensing` (CS) - Isolated high-precision shunt current sensor.
- **Module 4:** `high-voltage-power-supply` (HVPS) - Non-isolated HV buck converter for hot-side power.
- **Module 5:** `switching-circuit` (SWC) - Isolated low-side MOSFET switch array with integrated shunt.

**Connectors:**
- **J_CELLS:** 17-pin header for cell stack taps.
- **J_NTC:** 10-pin header for external thermistors.
- **J_HV:** Dedicated connectors for high-voltage bus (POS, NEG, PACK_NEG).
- **J_CTRL:** 13-pin connector for inter-board control interface.

## 4. Topology, Interconnect & Signal Flow

### 4.1 Power Distribution Nets
| Net Name | Origin | Destination(s) | Description |
|:---|:---|:---|:---|
| **HV_BUS_POS** | `J_HV_POS` | `HVPS.HV_IN_POS` | Traction Pack Positive (85V-400V). |
| **HV_BUS_NEG** | `J_HV_NEG` | `HVPS.HV_IN_NEG`, `SWC.BAT_NEG`, `SWC.GND_B`, `CS.GND1`, `BMM.CELL_TAP_0` | Traction Pack Negative / System HV Reference. |
| **PACK_NEG** | `SWC.PACK_NEG` | `J_PACK_NEG` | System Return (to Load/Charger). |
| **VDD1_ISO** | `HVPS.VDD1` | `CS.VDD1` | Isolated 5V rail for current sensing. |
| **VDD12V_ISO** | `HVPS.VDD12V`| `SWC.VDD_12V` | Isolated 12V rail for gate drivers. |
| **BAT_12V** | `J_CTRL` | `CB.BAT` | 12V Logic Supply from LVPS. |
| **VIO_3V3** | `J_CTRL` | `CB.VIO`, `CS.VDD2` | IO and Logic supply for cold-side. |
| **GND_LV** | `J_CTRL` | `CB.GND`, `CS.GND2`, `SWC.GND_LV` | Low-voltage system ground. |

### 4.2 Signal Interconnects
| Signal Group | From | To | Type |
|:---|:---|:---|:---|
| **Daisy Chain (Head)** | `CB.COMH_P/N` | `BMM.COM_LP/N` | Isolated Differential |
| **Current Sense Input** | `SWC.SRP/SRN` | `CS.INP/INN` | Kelvin Analog |
| **Cell Taps** | `J_CELLS` | `BMM.CELL_TAP_0-16` | Voltage Sense / Balancing |
| **Thermistors** | `J_NTC` | `BMM.NTC_CH1-8` | Analog Temperature Sensing |
| **Isolated Current Out**| `CS.OUT` | `J_CTRL.pin4` | Single-ended Analog |
| **Host Control (Comm)** | `CB.SPI/UART` | `J_CTRL.pin5-8` | Digital Communication |
| **Fault Indicator** | `CB.NFAULT` | `J_CTRL.pin13` | Open-drain Active Low |
| **Host Control (Switch)**| `J_CTRL.pin9/10`| `SWC.CTRL_CHG/DSG` | Isolated Logic Control |
| **Switch Status** | `SWC.STAT_CHG/DSG`| `J_CTRL.pin11/12` | Isolated Logic Status |

### 4.3 Pin-to-Pin Mapping (Module Integration)
| Port A (Source) | Port B (Destination) | Function |
|:---|:---|:---|
| `HVPS.VDD1` | `CS.VDD1` | Isolated Power Supply |
| `HVPS.VDD12V` | `SWC.VDD_12V` | Gate Driver Supply |
| `SWC.SRP` | `CS.INP` | Current Sense Positive (Kelvin) |
| `SWC.SRN` | `CS.INN` | Current Sense Negative (Kelvin) |
| `CB.COMH_P` | `BMM.COM_LP` | Daisy Chain High-Side Positive |
| `CB.COMH_N` | `BMM.COM_LN` | Daisy Chain High-Side Negative |
| `CB.NFAULT` | `J_CTRL.pin13` | System Fault indicator |

## 5. System Power Analysis
The following estimates reflect the total power consumption of the BMS (Control + Power circuits).

### 5.1 Power Rail Compatibility
| Power Rail | Primary Source | Capability | Max Sink | Margin | Result |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **VDD12V_ISO** | `HVPS` (Buck) | 225 mA | ~42 mA | **High** | **PASS** |
| **VDD1_ISO** | `HVPS` (LDO) | 100 mA | 8.5 mA | **High** | **PASS** |
| **VIO_3V3** | `LVPS` (LDO) | 800 mA | ~38 mA | **Excessive** | **PASS** |
| **BAT_12V** | `LVPS` (Flyback)| 2.0 A | ~20 mA | **Excessive** | **PASS** |

### 5.2 Estimated Total Power Consumption
| Domain | Typical | Worst-Case |
| :--- | :---: | :---: |
| **Traction Bus (Logic)** | 0.73 W | 1.15 W |
| **Cell Stack (Monitor)** | 0.78 W | 1.14 W |
| **Total BMS System** | **1.51 W** | **2.29 W** |

**Note:** Excludes passive balancing (~1.2W/cell).

## 6. Uncertainties, Engineering Assumptions & Risks
- **Daisy Chain Return:** In a single-module configuration, `BMM.COM_HP/N` may need to be looped back to `CB.COML_P/N` if a ring topology is desired for redundancy.
- **FET Thermal Performance:** The `SWC` handles up to 50A continuous. Proper heat sinking and copper pour area on the PCB are critical to prevent thermal runaway.
- **Isolation Rating:** The system relies on the isolation barriers within `CB` (transformers), `CS` (amplifier barrier), and `SWC` (optocouplers) to protect the LV domain.
- **Redundant VDD1:** The `BMM` offers a `CVDD` (5V) output which could serve as a redundant power source for `CS.VDD1`. This integration assumes the `HVPS` is the primary source.
- **NTC Sensor Integration:** [IN_PROGRESS] External thermistor inputs (`BMM.NTC_CH1-8`) are defined at the module boundary but are not yet routed to an external connector in this board revision.
- **NTC Sensor Insulation:** Since NTC sensors are connected to the HV-domain `BMM`, the sensors and their wiring must be rated for the maximum system voltage (400V) or otherwise isolated if they come into contact with the chassis or LV components.

